-- title:
--   Evaluations along one branch of a node multiply to a norm
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality hypotheses for the two Hecke maps, and a place specialisation $P$; let $R$ be a prolongation tuple for $P$ with $k$ perfect, and let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $\mathcal O := A \cap K$ for `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K` and $B :=$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` for the ring of those elements of the level-$Nq$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are integral for both prolongations $R_1, R_2$, lie in every valuation subring of a place $V$ with `P.reduceFst V = w`, and whose Laurent expansion lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K`. The data are: a place $w$ of the characteristic-$q$ modular function field of level $N$ over $k$, lying in `ssPlaces q N k`; node coordinates $c = (c.x, c.y)$ for $K$ and $w$; a nonzero $\varpi \in \mathcal O$; hypotheses that $B$ is local and noetherian with maximal ideal generated by the constant $\varpi$ together with $c.x$ and $c.y$, that every $g \in B$ differs from some constant of $\mathcal O$ by a non-unit, the value integrality law for $w$ (every element of the node-integer ring has all its values at places over $w$ in $A$), that every non-maximal prime of $B$ strictly above a prime forces the latter to be $\bot$, and that `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K` is the fraction field of $B$; a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ with irreducible $\pi$, an exponent $E \geq 1$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $B$ onto the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ with $\iota(\varpi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi$ and $\iota(c.x) = U \cdot \alpha_U$ for a unit $\alpha_U$; the assumption that $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$, and an isomorphism $\tau$ from its adic completion onto $W$ with $\tau(\varpi) = \pi$ and with $\iota$ carrying each constant $o \in \mathcal O$ to $\mathrm{const}(\tau(o))$; a nonzero prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ containing no nonzero constant; a ring homomorphism $j$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ to the valuation ring of the completion $C$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for the valuation of $A$, inducing on $\mathcal O$ the inclusion into $C$; an element $g \in B$; a finite set $S$ consisting exactly of the places $V$ of the level-$Nq$ field with `P.reduceFst V = w` whose evaluation kernel on $B$ is $\mathfrak q$, subject to the counting hypothesis that the cardinality of $S$ equals $\sum_Q \operatorname{finrank}_W$ of the quotient of the crossing model by $Q$, summed over the minimal primes $Q$ of the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ with $\mathrm{const}\,\pi \notin Q$; one such prime $Q$; and a finite set $S_Q$ consisting exactly of the $V \in S$ for which there is a ring homomorphism $\psi$ from the adic completion of $B$ to the valuation ring of $C$ agreeing with evaluation at $V$ on $B$ and with $\ker(\psi \circ \iota^{-1}) = Q$. The conclusion is the identity in $C$ $$\prod_{V \in S_Q} V.\mathrm{evalAt}(g) = j\bigl(\tau^{-1}(\mathrm{Norm}_{W}(\iota(g) \bmod Q))\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the per-branch product formula at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$: the places over $w$ with evaluation kernel $\mathfrak q$ that lie on the branch corresponding to a single minimal prime $Q$ of the crossing model contribute, through their values on $B$, exactly the $W$-norm of the image of the element in the quotient of the model by $Q$. It feeds the extraction of a place over $w$ with a prescribed value of the node coordinate $c.y$ in `exists_reduceFst_eq_and_evalAt_y_eq_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel`.
